bench-test live USB
===================

  bench-tui                       console dashboard (auto-starts on tty1)
  bench-gui                       graphical dashboard (X + mouse)
  bench-live-run                  plain console run (no dashboard)
  bench-collect                   copy results to the BENCHDATA USB partition
  bench-fan-curve status|set|off|check   GPU fan curve + fan-response test

The dashboard detects the GPU/CPU, offers presets (quick/full/graphics),
streams phase progress and live telemetry while running, shows the final
report, and collects everything to BENCHDATA when done.

Keys: s start · x stop · c collect · f fan-curve · p profile · 1-0 groups
      r report · G graphical dashboard · t shell · PgUp/PgDn log · q quit

Toolkit: /opt/bench-test        GPU tools: nvidia-smi / rocm-smi, FurMark in tools/furmark
